# What the chat-pane fix changes on purpose, and why.
#
# Run it as:
#   gate_diff.py --expect tools/porcelain_gate/expect/chat-pane.expect <pairs...>
#
# Do NOT concatenate this with gameframe-layout.expect. That file declares what
# the Porcelain PORT changed against the tree before the port landed; this fix
# branches from after it, so every line of it would be a stale declaration and
# a stale declaration fails the gate.
#
# Every line here is a claim a reader is meant to be able to disagree with. If
# you think one of them is wrong, the argument is with the reason, not with the
# tool.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One change, on the three lanes that put the desktop provider over an
# OldSchool chat pack: classic548, classic161 and remount164.
#
# Classic Fixed asked the lane how big its chatbox was, used the WIDTH it was
# given and threw the HEIGHT away, substituting the 2004 builtin's 96 rows. A
# 2004 chatbox is 96 rows because its geometry is fixed in the client's own
# code and reads nothing from its node; an OldSchool chatbox is interface 162,
# which lays itself out TO ITS BOX. Handed 96 rows it laid out a 73-row
# message window and showed THREE lines where the same lane's own frame shows
# eight, and then left fifty rows of bare rock under it.
#
# That is not a cosmetic difference and it is why this is declared rather than
# argued: a plugin notification is an ordinary game chat line, so a notice the
# player was meant to read scrolled out of a pane too short to hold it and
# never reached the screen. Both shipped NXT notification builtins fire
# correctly and neither was legible under this frame -- photographed in
# shots/frames/chatpane-birdnest-before.png against -after.png, with the
# lane's own frame beside them as the reference.
#
# So the pack now takes the 2004 ORIGIN and its own authored SIZE, flush with
# the canvas floor. Nothing else about the frame moves: the surround is
# unchanged, because the 2004 frame's own bottom band is already 165 rows deep
# (backhmid2 19 at y=338 + the chat hole 96 at y=357 + backbase1 50 at y=453)
# and the pack fills exactly it.

# The container the toplevel gives the pack. It is the one box this fix
# writes, and everything below is a consequence of it. One line per toplevel
# the three lanes open -- 548 (classic548), 161 (classic161) and 164
# (remount164, which switches to it half way through) -- because they are
# three spellings of one component: whichever root is live, the container is
# the layer interface 162 mounts into.
only-before BOUNDS com=0x0224000b (548|11) type=18 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=17,357 519x96 = the chatbox squeezed into the 2004 BUILTIN's 96 rows, which is the defect
only-after  BOUNDS com=0x0224000b (548|11) type=18 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=17,338 519x165 = and the 519x165 the lane authored, flush with the canvas floor
only-before BOUNDS com=0x00a10060 (161|96) type=18 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=17,357 519x96 = the same squeeze on toplevel 161
only-after  BOUNDS com=0x00a10060 (161|96) type=18 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=17,338 519x165 = and the same authored box on 161
only-before BOUNDS com=0x00a4005d (164|93) type=18 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=17,357 519x96 = the same squeeze on toplevel 164, after the remount lane switches layout
only-after  BOUNDS com=0x00a4005d (164|93) type=18 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=17,338 519x165 = and the same authored box on 164
role-move frame_chat = the same box, said about the role rather than the component

# Interface 162's whole subtree, because a pack given a different box lays
# itself out again. These two lines are the broadest declaration in this file
# and they are stated deliberately: the pack is the cache's own chatbox and
# its internal layout is script 924's, not this plugin's, so there is no
# smaller honest unit than "162 re-ran its layout". What bounds them is that
# they are the ONLY prefix in the diff besides the container above and the
# camera below -- checked, not assumed: grouping the whole bounds difference
# by interface gives 3222 lines of 162, one of 548 and one owned control.
only-before BOUNDS com=0x00a2 = the chat pack laid out for 96 rows
only-after  BOUNDS com=0x00a2 = the chat pack laid out for the 165 the lane gives it

# The pack's own furniture, each named. The backing is the message window and
# it is the whole point: 73 rows of it held three lines, 142 holds the eight
# the native frame shows. The bar and its eight plates drop 50 rows to y=480,
# which is inside `backbase1`'s strip -- where the 2004 frame's own filters
# stood, and where the lane's own frame puts this same bar.
role-move chat_backing = 519x73 held three chat lines; 519x142 holds the eight the lane's own frame shows
role-move chat_bar = the pack's stone bar moves to the floor with the pack, onto the strip the 2004 frame keeps its filters on
role-move chat_input = the typed line follows the message window it sits under
role-move chat_plate_0 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move chat_plate_1 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move chat_plate_2 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move chat_plate_3 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move chat_plate_4 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move chat_plate_5 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move chat_plate_6 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move chat_plate_7 = the filter plates ride the bar
role-move public_chat_button = the same plate, under the name the portable role table gives it
role-move report_button = the same plate, under the name the portable role table gives it
role-move action_frame_chat_button_report_activate = the same plate again, under its authored action name

# The screenshot plugin's camera is a REPLACE anchor on the Report button, so
# it goes where Report goes. It is the only owned control in the diff, and it
# moving is the anchor doing its job: a camera that stayed at y=433 while the
# button left would be the defect.
only-before BOUNDS com=0xffffffff (65535|65535) type=15 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=483,433 20x16 = the camera on the Report button's old seat
only-after  BOUNDS com=0xffffffff (65535|65535) type=15 graphic=-1 hidden=0 abs=483,483 20x16 = and on its new one, which is what a REPLACE anchor is for
owned-move camera_report = the same move said about the owned control: it moved because its REPLACE target moved, not for any reason of its own
